  "text": "In February of that year, most of us said the same four words: \"violence against women.\" At its peak 29 of us reached for that phrase on a single day, 28 for \"violence against women act,\" 26 for \"the violence against women.\" The record shows Maxine Waters saying it first, on the third of January, and the rest of us arriving behind her through the month toward the twenty-eighth.\n\nAlongside it, 16 of us spoke \"of domestic violence.\"\n\nA second, smaller convergence formed around the president's address: 19 of us said \"state of the union,\" 18 said \"of the union address,\" 17 the full \"state of the union address,\" clustering on the twelfth.\n\nTwo phrases, then, and we were most of us reading from them. We report this without comment. It is simply what the record holds.",
